sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as UI or strategy
    participant A as Command boundary
    participant E as Execution owner
    participant J as Durable journal
    participant P as Risk and mode policy
    participant B as Origin-specific broker
    participant R as Reconciliation

    U->>A: Submit intention with stable request ID
    A->>A: Validate schema, units, ownership and account context
    A->>E: Validated command
    E->>J: Insert intention if absent (unique request ID)
    J-->>E: New record or existing result
    alt Request already recorded
        E-->>U: Existing order status with no duplicate submission
    else New intention
        E->>P: Recheck arming, freshness and available exposure
        alt Admission denied
            E->>J: Persist rejection and reason
            E-->>U: Blocked with an actionable reason
        else Admission allowed
            E->>J: Commit reservation and SUBMITTING with stable client order ID
            Note over E,J: Transaction finishes before network I/O
            E->>B: Submit using persisted identity and origin
            alt Confirmed response
                B-->>E: Exchange ID, outcome and cumulative fill information
                E->>J: Persist normalized order state
                E-->>U: Confirmed current status
            else Timeout or ambiguous transport failure
                E->>J: Mark UNKNOWN and retain reserved exposure
                E-->>U: Outcome unresolved and reconciliation required
                E->>R: Resolve the existing intention
                R->>B: Read orders, fills and positions
                B-->>R: Exchange facts
                R->>E: Reconciled outcome or still unresolved
                E->>J: Apply evidence and keep unresolved reservations
                Note over E,B: No blind resubmission after an unknown outcome
            end
        end
    end

    Note over E,B: Private fills may arrive before or after the HTTP response
    B-->>E: Canonical fill or replayed fill event
    E->>J: Insert unique fill and update projections in one transaction
    Note over E,J: Duplicate fill IDs do not change inventory twice

    opt Operator stops a strategy
        U->>A: Stop quoting and cancel owned orders
        A->>E: Latch pause before further new submissions
        E->>J: Persist paused state and cancellation intentions
        E->>B: Cancel each real order using its stored origin
        B-->>E: Confirmed outcome, failure or timeout
        E->>J: Retain unresolved orders and reservations
        E-->>U: Quoting stopped with canceled / remaining / unresolved counts
        Note over E,B: Simulation settings never erase obligations for existing live orders
    end
